{"variant":"without","turns":[{"request":"Project \"Atlas\": an AI agentic platform for enterprises (users and apps, API gateway, orchestrator, planner and worker agents, tool gateway, model router, memory, retrieval, guardrails, human approval, observability, data stores). Draw its system architecture.","reply":"I drew Atlas top to bottom: users and apps go through the API gateway to the orchestrator and agents, then out through the model router and tool gateway to LLMs and enterprise tools. Guardrails and human approval sit on the left, memory, retrieval and data stores on the right, and observability spans all components along the bottom.","ok":true,"subtype":"success","durationMs":30143,"toolTurns":2,"outputTokens":3537},{"request":"Now add Atlas's technical documentation to the right of the architecture, one frame per document: agent execution flow, data model, API contract, security and guardrails, deployment, and non-functional requirements.","reply":"I added six frames to the right of the architecture, in a 3×2 grid: execution flow, data model, API contract, security and guardrails, deployment, and non-functional requirements. The endpoints, targets, compliance items and technology choices are my proposed defaults, so please check them against Atlas's real requirements.","ok":true,"subtype":"success","durationMs":35450,"toolTurns":2,"outputTokens":5760},{"request":"Now add a client presentation for Atlas below everything: 6 slides, one frame per slide, that a non-technical buyer can follow.","reply":"I added six slides in a 3×2 grid below everything: Meet Atlas, the challenge, how it works, staying in control, where it can help, and next steps. The use cases, safety promises and roughly 10-week pilot are my suggestions, so confirm them before showing a client.","ok":true,"subtype":"success","durationMs":28110,"toolTurns":2,"outputTokens":4172}],"ops":[{"turn":1,"op":"add","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"title","x":440,"y":-10,"text":"Atlas: Enterprise AI Ag